# Repo-wide: KSV-0056 flags write access to services, endpoints,
# endpointslices, networkpolicies and ingresses in any Role or ClusterRole.
# The operator creates and deletes the headless Services of multi-pod jobs.
# Review new networking grants by hand.
KSV-0056

# KSV-0048 flags create/delete on pods in a Role or ClusterRole. The operator
# schedules jobs by creating and deleting the pods that back them, so this is
# inherent to its function. The grant is scoped to pods only, not a wildcard.
KSV-0048

# DS-0026 flags a Dockerfile without a HEALTHCHECK. The image is multi-binary
# (spurctld, spurd, operator, CLI); health is defined per workload by the
# Kubernetes probes in examples/k8s/, not baked into the image.
DS-0026

# KSV-0125 flags images from registries outside Trivy's hardcoded trusted set.
# The examples pin the project's own published image (rocm/spur:<version>),
# which is the trusted source for this deployment. Pinning a versioned tag is
# the security goal; the registry policy cannot be satisfied for our own image.
KSV-0125
